      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:2:1:49:12",
      "text": [
        " إِنَّ اللَّهَ تَبَارَكَ وَ تَعَالَى لَيُعْطِي الْعَبْدَ مِنَ الثَّوَابِ عَلَى حُسْنِ الْخُلُقِ كَمَا يُعْطِي الْمُجَاهِدَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ يَغْدُو عَلَيْهِ وَ يَرُوحُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "And from him, from Bakr Bin Salih, from Al Hassan Bin Ali, from Abdullah Bin Ibrahim, from Ali Bin Abu Ali Al Lahby, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having sid: ‘Allah<sup>azwj</sup> Blessed and High would be Giving from the Rewards to the servant based upon the good manners, just as He<sup>azwj</sup> would Give to the fighter in the Way of Allah<sup>azwj</sup> (waking up) in the morning and going upon it’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "12. It is narrated from him (narrator of the Hadith above) from Bakr ibn Salih from al-Hassan ibn Ali from ‘Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim from Ali ibn abu Ali al-Lahabi from abu ‘Abd Allah (a.s.) who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah (a.s.) has said, ‘Allah, the Most Blessed, the Most High, grants good rewards to a person of excellent moral behavior as He grants rewards to one who strives hard (does Jihad) in the way of Allah, mornings and evenings.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
